# ChainShield Master Environment Setup Guide

This file contains the consolidated environment variable templates for all ChainShield services.
Copy this file to `.env` in the root directory and update with your actual credentials.

## Quick Setup

```bash
# Copy this file to .env
cp .env.example .env

# Edit .env with your actual credentials
# NEVER commit .env to Git!
```

---

## 🚀 Core Server Settings
NODE_ENV=development
PORT=5000
FRONTEND_URL=http://localhost:5173

# Ports for Docker Compose
BACKEND_PORT=5000
FRONTEND_PORT=5173
ML_SERVICE_PORT=5001
GRAPH_SERVICE_PORT=5002

---

## 📀 Database Settings (MongoDB)
# Initialization credentials
MONGO_ROOT_USERNAME=admin
MONGO_ROOT_PASSWORD=CHANGE_THIS_TO_A_STRONG_PASSWORD

# Backend Connection String
# Format: mongodb://[user]:[pass]@mongodb:27017/chainshield?authSource=admin
MONGODB_URI=mongodb://admin:CHANGE_THIS_TO_A_STRONG_PASSWORD@mongodb:27017/chainshield?authSource=admin

---

## 🛡️ Security Settings
# JWT Secret (Min 32 characters)
JWT_SECRET=CHANGE_THIS_TO_A_SECURE_RANDOM_STRING_MIN_32_CHARS
JWT_EXPIRE=24h

# TOTP 2FA Encryption Key (64 hex characters)
TOTP_ENCRYPTION_KEY=CHANGE_THIS_TO_A_64_HEX_CHARACTER_KEY

# Backup Encryption Key (AES-256)
BACKUP_ENCRYPTION_KEY=CHANGE_THIS_TO_A_64_HEX_CHARACTER_KEY

---

## 📧 Email Settings (SMTP)
SMTP_HOST=smtp.gmail.com
SMTP_PORT=587
SMTP_SECURE=false
SMTP_USER=your-email@gmail.com
SMTP_PASS=your-app-password
EMAIL_FROM=your-email@gmail.com
EMAIL_FROM_NAME=ChainShield

---

## ⛓️ Blockchain Settings (Ethereum/Ganache)
BLOCKCHAIN_RPC_URL=http://ganache:8545
CONTRACT_ADDRESS=YOUR_DEPLOYED_CONTRACT_ADDRESS_HERE

# Development Accounts (Ganache defaults)
BLOCKCHAIN_ACCOUNT=0xf39Fd6e51aad88F6F4ce6aB8827279cffFb92266
BLOCKCHAIN_PRIVATE_KEY=0xac0974bec39a17e36ba4a6b4d238ff944bacb478cbed5efcae784d7bf4f2ff80

# Ganache Mnemonic/Initialization
GANACHE_MNEMONIC=test test test test test test test test test test test junk
GANACHE_NETWORK_ID=1337

---

## 🤖 Service Coordination
ML_SERVICE_URL=http://ml-service:5001
GRAPH_SERVICE_URL=http://graph-service:5002

# SECURITY FIX (V3): Shared secret for internal ML service authentication
# Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
ML_API_SECRET=CHANGE_THIS_TO_A_SECURE_RANDOM_STRING

# Optional Redis (for persistent rate limiting across restarts)
REDIS_HOST=redis
REDIS_PORT=6379
REDIS_URL=redis://redis:6379

## 🗄️ MongoDB TLS (Production)
# SECURITY FIX (V6): Enable TLS for MongoDB connections in production
MONGODB_TLS=false
# MONGODB_TLS_CA_FILE=/path/to/ca.pem

---

## 🔑 Google OAuth / SSO
# Create credentials at: https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials
# Authorized redirect URI: http://localhost:5000/api/auth/google/callback (dev)
#                          https://your-domain.com/api/auth/google/callback (prod)
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=YOUR_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID_HERE
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=YOUR_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET_HERE
GOOGLE_CALLBACK_URL=http://localhost:5000/api/auth/google/callback

---

## 🚨 Security Checklist
- [ ] Change all default passwords/secrets
- [ ] Ensure `.env` is ignored by Git (checked via `git status`)
- [ ] Use `openssl rand -hex 32` to generate secure keys
- [ ] Set `MONGODB_TLS=true` for production deployments
- [ ] Set `ML_API_SECRET` to a strong random value
- [ ] Set `NODE_ENV=production` before deploying

